---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_vi4_442",
  "series": "Band VI 4 (1677 - 1690)",
  "seq": 442,
  "text": "[[1983.1]] <b>364.  Veritates physicae [Sommer 1678 bis Winter 1680/81 (?)]</b>\n [[1983.2]] <tab/>[Sommer 1678 bis Winter 1680/81 (?)] </p>\n<p> [[1983.6]] <p><k>Veritates</k> <k>Physicae</k> sunt vel <b>intellectuales</b> vel <b>sensuales</b> vel <b>mixtae.</b> </p>\n<p> [[1983.7]] <k>Intellectuales</k> sunt quae sola ratione cognoscuntur, suntque rursus vel <b>Axiomata</b>\n[[1983.8]] vel <b>Theoremata.</b> </p>\n<p> [[1983.9]] <k>Axiomata</k> sunt quae sine probatione assumi possunt, tanquam per se manifesta,\n[[1983.10]] exempli causa si duo gravia sint per omnia aequalia et similia,\n[[1983.11]] et suspendantur eodem modo a duobus brachiis aequalibus <i>ca,\n[[1983.12]] cb</i> ejusdem librae, erunt in aequilibrio. Hoc sane omnes\n[[1983.13]] admittent etiamsi non sint experti, nec alios expertos fuisse\n[[1983.14]] audiant, itaque est veritas intellectualis; neque postulabunt ut ratione aliqua confirmetur,\n[[1983.15]] itaque est axioma. </p>\n<p> [[1983.16]] <b>Theoremata</b> sunt veritates intellectuales quae ex aliis demonstrantur; exempli\n[[1983.17]] gratia si duo corpora gravia ejusdem materiae diversae magnitudinis suspendantur ex\n[[1983.18]] duobus brachiis quae sint inter se reciproce ut corporum ex iis suspensorum magnitu\n[[1984.1]] dines, erunt in aequilibrio; ut si pondus quidem <i>b</i> sit duplum\n[[1984.2]] ponderis <i>a</i>, sed brachium <i>cb</i> dimidium brachii <i>ca.</i> Haec propositio\n[[1984.3]] ex paulo ante dicta demonstratur assumtis quibusdam\n[[1984.4]] ratiociniis geometricis. </p>\n<p> [[1984.5]] Veritates physicae <k>sensuales</k> sunt quae solo sensu a\n[[1984.6]] nobis cognoscuntur; suntque vel <b>Historiae</b> vel <b>Inductiones.</b> </p>\n<p> [[1984.8]] <k>Historiae</k> sunt veritates sensuales singulares, ut relatio Eclipseos cujusdam lunaris. </p>\n<p> [[1984.9]] <k>Inductiones</k> sunt veritates sensuales universales ex pluribus singularibus consentientibus,\n[[1984.10]] suntque vel <b>observationes</b> vel <b>experimenta.</b> </p>\n<p> [[1984.11]] <k>Observationes</k> sunt inductiones ad quas tantum opus est ut spectatores agamus,\n[[1984.12]] tales sunt observationes coelestes, ut post diem semper sequi noctem; solis viam esse\n[[1984.13]] obliquam ad aequatorem, et alia id genus. </p>\n<p> [[1984.14]] <k>Experimenta</k> sunt inductiones, ubi non nudos spectatores agimus, sed corpora\n[[1984.15]] tractamus vel immutamus, talia sunt experimenta chymicorum. </p>\n<p> [[1984.16]] Inductiones habent suos gradus universalitatis, suntque aliae aliis certiores. Exempli\n[[1984.17]] gratia nemo prudens dubitat, quin cras sol sit oriturus; sed rhabarbarum purgare, non\n[[1984.18]] aeque certum est, aliquando enim fit ut nonnulli vix fortissimis medicamentis solicitentur.\n[[1984.19]] Saepe tamen contenti esse cogimur propositionibus plerumque veris, praesertim in Medicina.\n[[1984.20]] Nonnullae inductiones sunt plane insufficientes, et imprudenter illis fiditur. Exempli\n[[1984.21]] gratia, quoniam nautae notaverunt suo tempore nullam esse declinationem acus magneticae\n[[1984.22]] apud insulas Azores dictas, non ideo concludere debuerunt idem sequentibus temporibus\n[[1984.23]] futurum esse, nec proinde debuerunt hujus observationis causa primum meridianum\n[[1984.24]] per has insulas ducere. </p>\n<p> [[1984.25]] <k>Veritates mixtae</k> sunt quae partim ex sensualibus partim ex intellectualibus concluduntur.\n[[1984.26]] Exempli causa quod speculum concavum radios colligat, hoc pendet partim ex\n[[1984.27]] observatione sensu deprehensa, quod nimirum angulus incidentiae et reflexionis radii sint\n[[1984.28]] aequales, partim ex ratiociniis geometricis. </p>\n<p> [[1985.1]] Ubi notandum nos ratione quidem conjicere posse aequalitatem anguli incidentiae et\n[[1985.2]] reflexionis; imo, ubi naturam lucis cognoverimus, etiam demonstrare. Sed ad discendam\n[[1985.3]] lucis naturam prius opus est observationibus sensuum, ex quibus haec ipsamet de\n[[1985.4]] angulorum aequalitate, una esse potest. </p>\n<p> [[1985.5]] Patet etiam ex his eandem veritatem uni posse esse intellectualem, alteri sensualem,\n[[1985.6]] prout in ejus notitiam devenit. Notandum est etiam etsi in ratiocinationibus physicis saepe\n[[1985.7]] opus sit conjecturis, tamen ipsam conjectandi artem certis quibusdam regulis niti, quas\n[[1985.8]] etsi quandoque eventus destituat, plerumque tamen voto respondent; et prudentis viri\n[[1985.9]] officio functi sumus si eas sequamur. Serviunt vero hae conjecturae non tantum in usu\n[[1985.10]] vitae, sed etiam ut <b>facienda experimenta</b> nobis in mentem veniant quibus postea\n[[1985.11]] certi reddamur an recte conjecerimus; exempli causa quia spiritus ardens ex vino destillare\n[[1985.12]] potest, probabile erat eundem destillaturum et ex frumento et aliis, tentandum tamen\n[[1985.13]] erat antequam tuto crederetur: ita is qui observaverat aquam in antliis tantum ad triginta\n[[1985.14]] pedes elevari posse recte conjecit Hydrargyrum seu Mercurium vix ad totidem pollices\n[[1985.15]] elevatum iri, quia est plus quam duodecuplo gravior aqua; sed opus erat experimento ut\n[[1985.16]] securi redderemur, poterat enim haec elevationis terminatio ab alia longe causa quam\n[[1985.17]] liquoris gravitate oriri. </p>\n<p> [[1985.18]] Et hic quidem modus procedendi per conjecturas utramque in physicis et civilibus\n[[1985.19]] paginam facit, imo et in arithmetica et in geometria aliquando utilis est ad inveniendum\n[[1985.20]] etsi postea deprehenso successu certior probandi modus sit quaerendus. Est tamen ut dixi\n[[1985.21]] certa quaedam conjectandi seu conjecturae vim demonstrandi scientia, unde conjecturales\n[[1985.22]] quoque propositiones ad scientias pertinent. </p>\n",
  "number": "364.",
  "title": "Veritates physicae",
  "date": "[Sommer 1678 bis Winter 1680/81 (?)]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:364. Veritates physicae [Sommer 1678 bis Winter 1680/81 (?)] [Sommer 1678 bis Winter 1680/81 (?)] Veritates Physicae sunt vel intellectuales vel sensuales vel mixtae. Intellectuales sunt quae sola ratione cognoscuntur, suntque rursus vel Axiomata vel Theoremata. Axiomata sunt quae sine probatione as...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>